# The account the packaged service runs as, and the group its files
# belong to. Home is a state directory (screen(1) wants a writable home),
# not a login location: nologin keeps it unusable as an interactive
# account. Created by %sysusers_create_package in %pre.
u pidp8i - "PiDP-8/I simulator" /var/lib/pidp8i /sbin/nologin
g pidp8i -
# Deliberately no membership in the distribution's "gpio" group (same
# reasoning as the PiDP-10 packaging): "gpio" is every gpiochip on the
# machine, and the simulator only ever needs the SoC GPIO controller the
# panel is wired to.  pidp8i.rules (99-pidp8i.rules) re-tags just that
# one chip into this account's own group instead.  (The pinctrl backend
# used /dev/gpiomem, group gpio as well, but that device doesn't exist
# on the Fedora kernel at all; the chardev backend needs no group here
# beyond the rules file picking the right one.)
